   "boundaryReview": {
    "hodgsonTrack4": "VOB 14 (track 4, 300.0817 s, 28807840 frames) is complete on the disc: it opens with a ~6.5 s pulse intro after VOB 13's decay, and ends in a full fade-out (-51 to -54 dB RMS over its last 5 s) followed by 0.36 s of near-digital silence (-73.7 dB). Nothing is missing at either VOB boundary. The ~8 s shortfall against the 1984 CD (308.1 s) is in the content (a different, shorter edit or fade of this vinyl-sourced transfer), not a decoding or boundary loss.",
    "hodgsonTracks6and7": {
     "discStructure": "Track 6 = VOB 16 = 44409760 frames (462.6017 s); track 7 = VOB 17 = 46053280 frames (479.7217 s). The split is the VOB boundary; the disc's program chain, cell table and NAV packs all agree on it.",
     "audio": "Song 6's band stops at ~411.5-412 s into VOB 16 and decays by ~418 s. From ~418 s to the end of VOB 16 (44.6 s) is a continuous quiet passage (about -36 to -40 dB RMS, well above the ~-45 dB groove noise), with no silence or gap anywhere (no stretch below -50 dB for 0.25 s). A new harmonic layer enters softly at ~425.1 s (+2 dB, stereo image narrows), about 40,810,000 frames into VOB 16 (±10,000; the onset is gradual). Distinct note onsets begin at the VOB 16/17 boundary. VOB 17 opens with ~40 s of sparse quiet intro.",
     "conclusion": "The library split reproduces the disc exactly (bit-identical). Against the CD (425.1 / 516.6 s) the difference is where the quiet ~37.5 s passage is assigned: the CD index sits at the soft onset ~425.1 s into VOB 16 (37.5 + 479.72 = 517.2 s ≈ CD 516.6 s, the rest being vinyl run-out), the DVD at the start of VOB 17. Neither point is a silence gap. Moving the split would be an editorial choice, not a correction of decoded audio; if wanted, the candidate offset is ~40,810,000 frames into track 6 (to be confirmed by ear)."
    }
   },
